Dodge is the ability to anticipate your opponent's moves and avoid being
hit entirely. While everyone dodges to some extent, thieves have elevated
this to an art form. The best defense, after all, is simply not being
where the attack lands.

This passive skill provides a chance to completely avoid incoming attacks.
Higher skill levels increase both the frequency and reliability of
successful dodges. Unlike armor which reduces damage taken, a successful
dodge means taking no damage at all.

Dodge is particularly valuable for lightly-armored characters who cannot
rely on heavy protection. It complements other defensive abilities and
can mean the difference between life and death against powerful foes.

Note: The monk ability to avoid attacks through superior awareness has
been separated into a more advanced discipline known as Jirin.

Class: Thief
